{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if","id":1466468,"title":"[V5] What breaks if...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-03T08:35:43-07:00","id":1466468,"title":"[V5] What breaks if...","content":"We've started a V5 Chronicle now that there's STV support for the new edition (meaning there are more ways to incorporate the things we want). At the moment we're trying to give it a fair shot by playing RAW for several sessions before we move into homebrew territory.<br /> <br /> So, at the moment, I'm just noting the things that are problems (or that might escalate into problems) and thinking about how we might address them.<br /> <br /> We're the kind of table that rolls frequently (if it has a dice pool in the book, then we think it should be rolled), so obviously that impacts things that don't work as well if you don't Take Half a lot.<br /> <br /> The things below might be used in isolation or in combination, so I'm looking for things that break the game or have interactions I may not have foreseen.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, what breaks if...<br /> <br /> 1. ...instead of rouse check re-rolls (which have always felt clunky to us), you just ignore rouse costs on those Discipline levels instead? We roll enough for Messy Crits and Bestial Failures to be a thing anyway, and mostly just simplify those by adding +1 Hunger when nothing else is appropriate, so it's not as if Hunger won't ever go up. It will also make elders formidable, which seems appropriate, as they'll have free licence to use their Disciplines without cost at the highest levels of BP.<br /> <br /> If the above is too lenient, we could use the suggested rule from the book to only count every other rouse check. For re-rolls, just halve the rouse cost and round down before applying. I suspect you could track this easily using the slash and cross system (slash a Hunger box if the first rouse check was called for; cross it out if the second was called for). You'd then only roll Hunger Dice equal to the boxes fully X'd out.<br /> <br /> 2. ...instead of the complicated Blood Potency tables, there was an easily remembered formula for everything. Is it game-breaking if you just say that your rate of healing, Blood Surge, Discipline dice bonus and Bane Severity are all exactly equal to your Blood Potency? The only exception would need to be rouse re-rolls, at half your BP, rounded up; and Thin Bloods, who get a minimum rating of 1 for healing and Blood Surge.<br /> <br /> 3. ...instead of human-only Touchstones, you can pick non-mortal Touchstones at the cost of -1 Humanity at the start of play (for each non-human Touchstone). Is that too harsh a trade-off?<br /> <br /> 4. ...instead of mandatory Touchstones and Convictions, you make them Backgrounds that mitigate Humanity loss, but you otherwise use the Humanity and Paths from V20 with the V5 Stains and Remorse system.<br /> <br /> 5. ...Hunger could be applied in two ways? Let's call these Gnawing and Goading Hunger. Gnawing Hunger eats up your regular dice pool in the way we're familiar with, and represents the Beast impinging upon activities that do not directly feed its needs. <br /> <br /> Goading Hunger, though, is a bit more seductive. It's the Beast increasing your power to undertake the things it wants you to do: violence, feeding, hunting, seduction, etc. On these rolls, you add your Hunger Dice, instead of replacing standard dice. This represents the Beast encouraging your behaviour and giving you a greater dice pool (with the increased risk of Messy Criticals that creates).<br /> <br /> 6. ...we say that Bestial Failures are only when you fail a roll with Gnawing Hunger and at least one Hunger Die comes up with a 1. Similarly, Messy Criticals only occur if you roll a critical on a roll with Goading Hunger Dice, rather than with Gnawing Hunger Dice. <br /> This makes these rarer. You could make it even rarer by saying you need to roll more successes overall on such a roll than your Composure (and still get a 10 on a Hunger Dice). That reflects 'losing control' and overachieving because of the Beast's goading.<br /> <br /> 7. ...Resonance only granted Willpower. If your victim's Resonance fits your current Ambition or Desire, you regain 1wp for every Hunger slaked.<br /> <br /> 8. ...you replaced Blood Surge with something a bit more deadly. Instead, you rouse the blood and can take any number of extra Goading Hunger Dice (up to a maximum bonus of twice your Hunger) for the next roll. This could lead to quite epic actions at the risk of loss of control.<br /> <br /> 9. ...keeping the usual Blood Surge mechanics, you instead let the bonus apply to a single Attribute for a whole scene. You can buff multiple Attributes this way.<br /> <br /> 10. ...Bane Severity were replaced by the VTR method (e.g., based off Humanity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T08:55:54-07:00","id":1466471,"title":"","content":"And a new one:<br /> <br /> What breaks if...<br /> <br /> 11. ...BP acts as a cap on traits (minimum 5 for all). So elders can have superhuman traits again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T09:01:12-07:00","id":1466473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. ...instead of human-only Touchstones, you can pick non-mortal Touchstones at the cost of -1 Humanity at the start of play (for each non-human Touchstone). Is that too harsh a trade-off?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, I'm a proponent of human-only touchstones. Humans, unlike objects, have agency. They get into trouble on their own, change on their own, interact with the world on their own. Humans can have relationships and opinions on a vampire that keeps stalking them for decades. With objects you just shove them into a vault and call it a day. Shoving your human touchstone into a vault tells a whole story of its own.<br /> <br /> But the question is - do you even want Touchstones? If your vampire story isn't going to have PCs spurred into action by the involvement of the Touchstones, if Touchstones exist purely as something the PC interacts with during downtime - why bother? Just drop the whole mechanic. Give every vampire 1-3 Convictions, let them change when narratively relevant, and call it a day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T09:26:12-07:00","id":1466475,"title":"","content":"Number 3 is a really good idea but loose the penalty as long as its a morality rather than emotionally affirmative touchstone<br /> <br /> Might is also suggest losing the negative effects of oblivion? While thematically neat it's basically an additional clan flaw for hecteta and lasombra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T09:50:14-07:00","id":1466482,"title":"","content":"2. How many different Blood Potencies are you interacting with on the regular for checking the table once in a while to be an issue? After BP is higher than 3, vampire get way more powerful.<br /> <br /> 3. I recommend not picking any touchstones and just going with a low humanity once stains start happening.<br /> <br /> Take care with giving too much dice, as when dice pools get too high, almost every roll becomes a critical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T10:33:15-07:00","id":1466490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1466473#post1466473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, I'm a proponent of human-only touchstones. Humans, unlike objects, have agency. They get into trouble on their own, change on their own, interact with the world on their own. Humans can have relationships and opinions on a vampire that keeps stalking them for decades. With objects you just shove them into a vault and call it a day. Shoving your human touchstone into a vault tells a whole story of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of storytelling opportunities that could come from Touchstones that aren't individual humans -- such as places, relics, businesses or even a whole family.<br /> <br /> As written, Touchstones just feel like dead weight. You're creating all these NPCs, alongside Contacts, Herd, Allies, etc, which the ST has to manage and which probably won't end up being used that often anyway. In some cases, it's a case of players feeling saddled with humans that don't really fit their concepts either.<br /> <br /> If, by opening up Touchstones, it allows players (and me as the ST) to create facets of the game we'll actually want to engage with, and which fit our concepts, then it's worth doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the question is - do you even want Touchstones? If your vampire story isn't going to have PCs spurred into action by the involvement of the Touchstones, if Touchstones exist purely as something the PC interacts with during downtime - why bother? Just drop the whole mechanic. Give every vampire 1-3 Convictions, let them change when narratively relevant, and call it a day. </div> </div> </div>I guess that's a nice and easy way to do it. My preference would probably be to allow people to take optional Touchstones (human or not), but just separate the need for them to be tied to Convictions. They're a story hook that can give some benefits for avoiding degeneration, but no one feels they've been foisted with NPCs they aren't interested in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Might is also suggest losing the negative effects of oblivion? While thematically neat it's basically an additional clan flaw for hecteta and lasombra </div> </div> </div>Good shout. I'm likely to separate Oblivion back into Necromancy and Obtenebretion anyway. As a Wraith player, I feel the Abyss should never have been conflated with the Underworld. Obtenebretion loses so much that way and you end up with some weird results (Hecata with Obtenebretion, Lasombra with Necromancy) that undermines the feel of both clans. (YMMV, etc.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1466482#post1466482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. How many different Blood Potencies are you interacting with on the regular for checking the table once in a while to be an issue? After BP is higher than 3, vampire get way more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the book is just such a nightmare, organisation-wise, I want to reduce *any* requirement to look things up. Also, since day 1, I've felt the Blood Potency table is a convoluted mess designed to evoke the flexibility of a larger blood pool without being a blood pool. It offends my mind somehow and I can't quite explain it.<br /> <br /> That said, it also helps with making NPCs on the fly. I'm a pantser, rather than a planner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take care with giving too much dice, as when dice pools get too high, almost every roll becomes a critical. </div> </div> </div>I thought about that and had considered using the VTR definition of a critical instead (i.e., 5+ successes; pairs of 10s can still double, as before). For a Messy Critical, you'd still need one 10 on a Hunger Dice. I might just do that if adding dice becomes a problem.<br /> <br /> I probably won't stack the dice adding rules. I'll probably just choose one rule that buffs vampires a bit across the board, so they're less puny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-03-2021, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:17:22-07:00","id":1466670,"title":"","content":"My take on this is as yet untested, but based on general observations:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. ...instead of rouse check re-rolls (which have always felt clunky to us), you just ignore rouse costs on those Discipline levels instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how the characters will use their Disciplines. At first nothing breaks, but ignoring any cost is like putting a spamming button on Disciplines.<br /> <br /> You just have to take that into account. If it seems like a problem, then trading double rouse for 2 or 3 uses before rousing is enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. ...instead of the complicated Blood Potency tables, there was an easily remembered formula for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its easier to transcribe the table somewhere. But that aside, it actually <b>is</b> an easily remembered formula! Te only difference is that it isn't Thing = BP, but Thing = \u00bd BP. Half of those things round up, half round down, so you have half of the effects increasing at even BP and half increasing at odd BP.<br /> <br /> Making it Thing = BP will make a far bigger increase in power from one BP to another, and that's especially relevant as now you have a range of BP inside each Generation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. ...instead of human-only Touchstones, you can pick non-mortal Touchstones at the cost of -1 Humanity at the start of play (for each non-human Touchstone). Is that too harsh a trade-off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely too harsh a trade-off.<br /> <br /> If you decide that non-human Touchstones work for you, just do it. If you decide your game doesn't need Touchstones just do it.<br /> <br /> As a mechanic they're thematic, not necessary, so nothing at all breaks when you change them to be worth a penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. ...instead of mandatory Touchstones and Convictions, you make them Backgrounds that mitigate Humanity loss</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already what they are.<br /> <br /> V5's Humanity is an excellent rule with a poor presentation that fails to easily describe how it works.<br /> <br /> What makes or brakes it is your choice of Chronicle Tenets. It is perfectly possible to determine that your Tenets are the Hierarchy of Sins of any Path you want, and it is also perfectly fine to decide that each character have its own Tenets instead.<br /> <br /> But by doing so you may be loosing on actual interesting possibilities to better define your chronicle, as now you can add or subtract &quot;sins&quot; to fit your themes.<br /> <br /> Convictions are exactly like Merits that help you to keep your Humanity, nothing else, and they're not so much Mandatory. I think you should keep them as is, as 1 to 3 is a pretty fair number, but by all means you can decide to create a Merit if you want a player to have more. A player that don't want any Conviction is also perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> Touchstones exist to force characters to interact with mortals in their keeping of their Humanity and color it by their Convictions. They don't help directly, just anchor Convictions, but it is just a thematic rule that you can change freely.<br /> <br /> On my side, I think it is kind of self-evident why they are tied to Humans, but changing it to anything else is pretty common. The big thing with them is how you define <i>Harm</i> and <i>Destruction</i>. I think that ignoring the RAW on that part and customizing those definitions for each case is the best way to get the most out of them for the least trouble with rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. ...Hunger could be applied in two ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would change a lot of what Hunger have always been in the game, and change a lot of rules.<br /> <br /> So my take on this is that no one can really predict how those options will affect your game. This is a very big homebrew.<br /> <br /> Instead of applying them as you thought them right away, experiment first with the game as is, then add those options with care. They'll change many rules and rules interactions, and increase the bookkeeping in your game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. ...we say that Bestial Failures are only when you fail a roll with Gnawing Hunger and at least one Hunger Die comes up with a 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first impression is the game counts on dice-generated complications to reduce other rules for triggering stuff. I may be wrong, but I would try it out before concluding that they happen too frequently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. ...Resonance only granted Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance is another thematic rule. It exists for players to have more to interact with in their feeding. Simplifying is perfectly valid, but I think they add a nice touch as they are, so I wouldn't recommend doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. ...you replaced Blood Surge with something a bit more deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the current rules I think their deadliness is on-spot. If you change the Attribute maximum, then it may be worth it to increase their potency just a little.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9. ...keeping the usual Blood Surge mechanics, you instead let the bonus apply to a single Attribute for a whole scene. You can buff multiple Attributes this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable to me. I like the rules, I don't like their duration. But you'll have to take a look at Disciplines just to be sure this is balanced with dedicated powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. ...Bane Severity were replaced by the VTR method (e.g., based off Humanity).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing breaks, but themes change. As is, Bane Severity acts as a <i>Price of Power</i> theme, which reinforces the difference between Neonates and the powerful Elders.<br /> <br /> Making it be based on Humanity will change the theme to <i>Risks of Evil</i>, and creates a new mechanic incentive to stay at High Humanity. You may go another route and, following closer to original but unsupported themes in VtM, make it related to age, giving it a <i>Price of Immortality</i> twist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">11. ...BP acts as a cap on traits (minimum 5 for all). So elders can have superhuman traits again.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sincerely not sure. On one hand I'm as taken aback as everyone else by their lack of superhuman traits. On the other hand I'm not sure it was actually a good idea to begin with.<br /> <br /> One way or another the current scheme keeps elders more manageable in terms of numbers/dice, and I think mechanics like double Hunger rolls are better than just moar dice.<br /> <br /> Can't say it isn't a worthy idea to try out, but I think that looking for other ways to highlight their greater power may have an actually better pay off.<br /> <br /> Another ever present question is how much those characters can still be meaningfully interacted with from a rules perspective. Trait Inflation makes it hard to believe in some events in the lore where Kindred of less age and higher generation explored elders' weaknesses as the rules actually make it too hard anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:46:28-07:00","id":1466690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. ...instead of mandatory Touchstones and Convictions, <b>you make them Backgrounds</b> that mitigate Humanity loss, but you otherwise use the Humanity and Paths from V20 with the V5 Stains and Remorse system<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What break: You need Touchstone to raise your Humanity in v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 11-04-2021, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:51:00-07:00","id":1466713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1466690#post1466690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What break: You need Touchstone to raise your Humanity in v5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you decide you don't, which is likely if you're removing them to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T16:50:43-07:00","id":1466724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if#post1466468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've started a V5 Chronicle now that there's STV support for the new edition (meaning there are more ways to incorporate the things we want). At the moment we're trying to give it a fair shot by playing RAW for several sessions before we move into homebrew territory..</div> </div> </div> </div>So big long reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. ...instead of rouse check re-rolls (which have always felt clunky to us), you just ignore rouse costs on those Discipline levels instead? We roll enough for Messy Crits and Bestial Failures to be a thing anyway, and mostly just simplify those by adding +1 Hunger when nothing else is appropriate, so it's not as if Hunger won't ever go up. It will also make elders formidable, which seems appropriate, as they'll have free licence to use their Disciplines without cost at the highest levels of BP. </div> </div> </div>Completely removing Rouse Checks removes an element of randomness, but also outright guarantees those who can ignore the Rouse Checks have a an unbeatable advantage, because they have one less thing to increase their Hunger. It'll mess with the 'core' math, simply because characters with a lower BP will still be rolling, and will get to a point of Hunger Frenzies or not being able to Rouse much faster than those of higher BP. It might be what you want, but it'll contribute to what we've called Unbeatable Elder Syndrome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the above is too lenient, we could use the suggested rule from the book to only count every other rouse check. For re-rolls, just halve the rouse cost and round down before applying. I suspect you could track this easily using the slash and cross system (slash a Hunger box if the first rouse check was called for; cross it out if the second was called for). You'd then only roll Hunger Dice equal to the boxes fully X'd out. </div> </div> </div>That's not a terrible way to track that, and it will mess with the core math a whole lot less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. ...instead of the complicated Blood Potency tables, there was an easily remembered formula for everything. Is it game-breaking if you just say that your rate of healing, Blood Surge, Discipline dice bonus and Bane Severity are all exactly equal to your Blood Potency? The only exception would need to be rouse re-rolls, at half your BP, rounded up; and Thin Bloods, who get a minimum rating of 1 for healing and Blood Surge. </div> </div> </div>It's going to, again, screw with the core math and how Criticals function. It'll also (again) commit even more into the Unbeatable Elder Syndrome. When you have a BP4 Elder versus a BP1 character, that would be 3 dice of difference, which stacked with everything else, such as the DPB, becomes +6 dice on Discipline activation and some other things. Or healing 1 damage versus healing 4 damage. You can stack things to a point of literally unbeatable based on the dice, unless the lower stat characters are fishing for criticals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. ...instead of human-only Touchstones, you can pick non-mortal Touchstones at the cost of -1 Humanity at the start of play (for each non-human Touchstone). Is that too harsh a trade-off? </div> </div> </div>That's more of a group comfortability thing. It kind of veers away from what Humanity in V5 is supposed to represent (a How I Am Not The Beast Meter, representative of you being actively reminded of Why You Aren't The Beast), but it won't actively break anything. This is actually more punishing than just allowing non-Human Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. ...instead of mandatory Touchstones and Convictions, you make them Backgrounds that mitigate Humanity loss, but you otherwise use the Humanity and Paths from V20 with the V5 Stains and Remorse system. </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you're just chucking in Paths and stuff with their much larger arrangement of 'sins' then it's less of a break than even the above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. ...Hunger could be applied in two ways? Let's call these Gnawing and Goading Hunger. Gnawing Hunger eats up your regular dice pool in the way we're familiar with, and represents the Beast impinging upon activities that do not directly feed its needs.<br /> <br /> Goading Hunger, though, is a bit more seductive. It's the Beast increasing your power to undertake the things it wants you to do: violence, feeding, hunting, seduction, etc. On these rolls, you add your Hunger Dice, instead of replacing standard dice. This represents the Beast encouraging your behaviour and giving you a greater dice pool (with the increased risk of Messy Criticals that creates). </div> </div> </div>This is really, really fiddly from a tracking standpoint. You'd also have to figure out what gives Gnawing versus Goading Hungers and all the things that spiral out from there, such as how to decrease, do different things decrease different types, etc. And the increased dice pools of Goading Hunger are going to continue to throw off the math unless things are roughly equivalent in places.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. ...we say that Bestial Failures are only when you fail a roll with Gnawing Hunger and at least one Hunger Die comes up with a 1. Similarly, Messy Criticals only occur if you roll a critical on a roll with Goading Hunger Dice, rather than with Gnawing Hunger Dice.<br /> This makes these rarer. You could make it even rarer by saying you need to roll more successes overall on such a roll than your Composure (and still get a 10 on a Hunger Dice). That reflects 'losing control' and overachieving because of the Beast's goading. </div> </div> </div>Beyond the fiddly bits above, this is more of a comfortability choice. If you want less Messy Criticals, you'd be better off doing the 'take every other Rouse' thing rather than building something brand new that has to be separately stress-tested with the math.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. ...Resonance only granted Willpower. If your victim's Resonance fits your current Ambition or Desire, you regain 1wp for every Hunger slaked. </div> </div> </div>This makes Willpower the new 'mana bar,' and also is actually more to track than the current Resonance system (since right now you just need to track whether it gives you a dice bonus or not, rather than if it matches your Ambition and Desire and then also fill up a bar). It also makes Willpower less of a 'risk versus reward' resource, and minimizes powers like Dementation that effect Willpower (which is why they're useful and powerful).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8. ...you replaced Blood Surge with something a bit more deadly. Instead, you rouse the blood and can take any number of extra Goading Hunger Dice (up to a maximum bonus of twice your Hunger) for the next roll. This could lead to quite epic actions at the risk of loss of control. </div> </div> </div>Math will break, mainly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. ...keeping the usual Blood Surge mechanics, you instead let the bonus apply to a single Attribute for a whole scene. You can buff multiple Attributes this way. </div> </div> </div>Math will break. Math will break in even more unexpected ways since you can Blood Surge any Attribute roll in V5, not just the physicals. It'll make things like Ritual activations extremely trivial. It'll make combat into rocket tag (and probably not even that, if the numbers gulf is deep enough). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10. ...Bane Severity were replaced by the VTR method (e.g., based off Humanity). </div> </div> </div>So how would that work with the 'scaling up' of Bane Severity? Lower humanity = higher Bane Severity? I'm not familiar with Requiem 2e. It feels like it would work, but you'd remove any downside to high BP really, which is part of why Elders play the Jyhad the way they do, from a narrative standpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11. ...BP acts as a cap on traits (minimum 5 for all). So elders can have superhuman traits again. </div> </div> </div>Math breaks.<br /> <br /> V5's math is built to function well up to around 15 total dice, then as you scale beyond that, and as you creep up on 20 and move beyond 20 you start getting into Mathematically Unbeatable territory, based on the averages and the different dice adds, even with V5's core mechanics. If you let stats go to 6+, have surges last the whole turn and buff an Attribute rather than a roll, and scale up the dice adds from BP, you are basically front-loading any high BP character towards this mathematically untouchable state. That's not even including things like the BP caps for gen, which messes with the math even more.<br /> <br /> I posted some math on the forum before about a BP2 versus a BP7 character with old style attributes of 6+, and even without the extra adds from different things in this 'what if' post, it became mathematically unbeatable at a point. It would just get worse with the additional adds listed here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 11-04-2021, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T00:56:24-07:00","id":1466752,"title":"","content":"Ah, so I think I haven't explained Gnawing versus Goading Hunger properly. The idea is that you still only have one Hunger rating, it's just that you replace dice on some rolls (e.g., those that require concentration) and you add it to others (e.g., those that make you deadly). It's exactly the same accounting method. What's different is the ST might say, &quot;Add your Hunger Dice this time&quot; instead of &quot;Replace black dice with red dice.&quot;<br /> <br /> My thinking here is that, RAW, if you have a dice pool made up entirely of Hunger Dice, you can't re-roll them, and in moments of crisis this makes you less likely to succeed at some of the things the Beast would seem to want to encourage, such as murdering your enemies or hunting for prey.<br /> <br /> Paired with VTR2e's Critical rules (so a Critical is 5+ successes), this would then increase your chance of Messy Crits on those rolls but make you more dangerous overall.<br /> <br /> Goading Hunger would probably replace Blood Surge and the Discipline dice pool bonus, though. Having all three would probably be unnecessary. Basically, Goading Hunger is a bit more like taking Shadow Dice in Wraith.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'm not worried about Unbeatable Elder Syndrome. I actually think that's a plus. But if I went with a boost in one area, I wouldn't add in all the others.<br /> <br /> That leads me to another idea, though. We could just allow re-rolls of Hunger Dice, provided they're not &quot;fixed&quot; with a 1 or a 10 already. That would get around the issue of a character who rolls all Hunger Dice on an attack and therefore can't re-roll, thus failing at something the Beast would want them to do. It also means you increase your chance of a Messy Crit or Bestial Failure on those rolls.<br /> <br /> In regards to rouse checks and things, I think we want to keep hunting to once per session. We will have to think of some way to limit spiralling Hunger in the end, I think. But I'll see how things pan out.<br /> <br /> As for Resonance: I'm not afraid of the 'mana bar'. It's neutral as a game mechanic, IMO, and the way people talk about it can definitely be quite snobby. Also, I have no problem with making superficial Willpower easier to regain within sessions (rather than between them), but I think, having slept on it, I'll probably key it off something else (Desire and Ambition seem hard to fit with Resonance on the fly). I think I will just take the V5 recommendation to reward players with WP for taking Compulsions. That might be enough.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the helpful info, folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-05-2021, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T09:32:43-07:00","id":1466777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1466752#post1466752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so I think I haven't explained Gnawing versus Goading Hunger properly. The idea is that you still only have one Hunger rating, it's just that you replace dice on some rolls (e.g., those that require concentration) and you add it to others (e.g., those that make you deadly). It's exactly the same accounting method. What's different is the ST might say, &quot;Add your Hunger Dice this time&quot; instead of &quot;Replace black dice with red dice.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks for clarifying. Yeah, that wasn't clear, it sounded like you had separate things to futz with. So it's basically 'based on the type of roll, the Hunger does different things'. That's not anywhere near as fiddly then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My thinking here is that, RAW, if you have a dice pool made up entirely of Hunger Dice, you can't re-roll them, and in moments of crisis this makes you less likely to succeed at some of the things the Beast would seem to want to encourage, such as murdering your enemies or hunting for prey.<br /> <br /> Paired with VTR2e's Critical rules (so a Critical is 5+ successes), this would then increase your chance of Messy Crits on those rolls but make you more dangerous overall.<br /> <br /> Goading Hunger would probably replace Blood Surge and the Discipline dice pool bonus, though. Having all three would probably be unnecessary. Basically, Goading Hunger is a bit more like taking Shadow Dice in Wraith. </div> </div> </div>I did miss the part where further down you mentioned using VtR's critical methods. If you're doing that, I'd also recommend dropping the crit pairing = 4 successes, and use the normal '10s explode infinitely' angle, assuming 2e still does that. It will make a Messy potentially more messy if you apply it to the 10s necessary for Messy Criticals, but removing the crit pairing will overall reduce the numbers of them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overall, I'm not worried about Unbeatable Elder Syndrome. I actually think that's a plus. But if I went with a boost in one area, I wouldn't add in all the others. </div> </div> </div>Just be cognizant of the math and you'll be fine. If you were to do any of the bonuses, I'd simply do the stat cap removal and nothing else. DPB stacks itself well enough already, and changing BP bonuses is going to effect multiple math points because of how it effects surge, DPB and others. Changing the surge amount/duration will still trivialize a lot of things even when not paired with the rest of the adds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That leads me to another idea, though. We could just allow re-rolls of Hunger Dice, provided they're not &quot;fixed&quot; with a 1 or a 10 already. That would get around the issue of a character who rolls all Hunger Dice on an attack and therefore can't re-roll, thus failing at something the Beast would want them to do. It also means you increase your chance of a Messy Crit or Bestial Failure on those rolls. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I like that rerolling non-1/10 Hunger dice angle with WP, and the extra stress that can cause in general. I will say I've rarely seen a character roll a whole pool of nothing but Hunger dice, unless it was a roll in a situation they were completely unprepared for, but it is a concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In regards to rouse checks and things, I think we want to keep hunting to once per session. We will have to think of some way to limit spiralling Hunger in the end, I think. But I'll see how things pan out. </div> </div> </div>I'll ponder on some things. I don't tend to find spiraling Hunger to be as big of an issue as some people do, as I have had games go without needing Rouse Checks at all, and I've had games where Rouse Checks happened a lot but we never had many Messy/Bestial. RNG likes my normal playgroup apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Resonance: I'm not afraid of the 'mana bar'. It's neutral as a game mechanic, IMO, and the way people talk about it can definitely be quite snobby. Also, I have no problem with making superficial Willpower easier to regain within sessions (rather than between them), but I think, having slept on it, I'll probably key it off something else (Desire and Ambition seem hard to fit with Resonance on the fly). I think I will just take the V5 recommendation to reward players with WP for taking Compulsions. That might be enough. </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to sound dismissive or snobby, so that's my bad there. And making it easier to regain is fine, but it does minimize the usefulness of certain powers and abilities. A lot of people have said they had success with WP for compulsions, and I have always used the 'acting towards your Desire restores WP'. It helps keep players on their own tracks, or keeps them having their tracks involved in the main story in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T00:31:38-07:00","id":1466912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1466777#post1466777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thanks for clarifying. Yeah, that wasn't clear, it sounded like you had separate things to futz with. So it's basically 'based on the type of roll, the Hunger does different things'. That's not anywhere near as fiddly then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I was thinking more like Shadow Dice, but also like the Free League Stress Dice. If Hunger Dice can be positive as well as negative, that just makes the temptation theme stronger, IMO. Hunger becomes something seductive as well as punitive, and that may encourage players to think, &quot;Well I'll probably fail at the cool and calm solution, so I'll do something dangerous and violent instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did miss the part where further down you mentioned using VtR's critical methods. If you're doing that, I'd also recommend dropping the crit pairing = 4 successes, and use the normal '10s explode infinitely' angle, assuming 2e still does that. It will make a Messy potentially more messy if you apply it to the 10s necessary for Messy Criticals, but removing the crit pairing will overall reduce the numbers of them. </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking, too. So a Messy Crit would be 5+ successes across any dice, with at least one 10 on a Hunger Die. Much rarer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just be cognizant of the math and you'll be fine. If you were to do any of the bonuses, I'd simply do the stat cap removal and nothing else. DPB stacks itself well enough already, and changing BP bonuses is going to effect multiple math points because of how it effects surge, DPB and others. Changing the surge amount/duration will still trivialize a lot of things even when not paired with the rest of the adds. </div> </div> </div>Duly noted. I will try to limit changes and see how we get on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I like that rerolling non-1/10 Hunger dice angle with WP, and the extra stress that can cause in general. I will say I've rarely seen a character roll a whole pool of nothing but Hunger dice, unless it was a roll in a situation they were completely unprepared for, but it is a concern. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think it's a rare occurrence. You'd probably be more likely to see a dice pool where the Hunger Dice all come up blank and where you only have two or fewer normal dice to reroll. In that case, re-rolling a Hunger Die might give you a better shot, and it will definitely make things more dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll ponder on some things. I don't tend to find spiraling Hunger to be as big of an issue as some people do, as I have had games go without needing Rouse Checks at all, and I've had games where Rouse Checks happened a lot but we never had many Messy/Bestial. RNG likes my normal playgroup apparently. </div> </div> </div>As I say, I think we are used to rolling more than this game requires to work. We've also been playing 1-on-1, so it puts more focus on the one PC to do everything. But no sooner had he fed than he'd gone back up to Hunger 2 within about 20 minutes. That was the point he started feeling that the game was working against him, not with him.<br /> <br /> Mind you, we had this exact same problem with WFRP3e and he's not overly keen on Alien/Free League for the same reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't mean to sound dismissive or snobby, so that's my bad there. And making it easier to regain is fine, but it does minimize the usefulness of certain powers and abilities. A lot of people have said they had success with WP for compulsions, and I have always used the 'acting towards your Desire restores WP'. It helps keep players on their own tracks, or keeps them having their tracks involved in the main story in some way. </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's okay. It happens.<br /> <br /> V5 definitely has less room for fiddling about with things. I think if we end up in a place where we love some things and don't like others, instead of extensive house rules it would just be easier to go back to V20 and add in what we do like. V20, whether you love it or hate it, has fewer interdependent parts, which makes it a more stable chassis for homebrew. E.g., the V20DA combat system makes for a very fast and deadly style of combat, but it also has tactical depth if you need it.<br /> <br /> Things we like from V5 include Messy Criticals, Bestial Failures and Compulsions (in moderation); the tweaked Advantages and Loresheets (though the organisation of these is a tad messy); that the Discipline powers are much more balanced, though generally you need more of them than in V20 to be powerful and we'd probably end up removing the limit of one per dot; fixed target numbers, although we've been using those for a while anyway; and the new Attributes (which have grown on me).<br /> <br /> I'm not overly fond of WP damage for social combat. Mainly because the modifiers seem skewed towards public humiliation rather than leverage, and this is pretty much the opposite of Exalted 3e's Intimacies system (which is my favourite social combat system ever). But I think I can work with this.<br /> <br /> Combat is fast, but I'm neutral on it. The book is badly organised and doesn't explain it well, but the V5 combat primer is much more helpful in that regard. I can definitely see the attraction of combat that's done in five minutes instead of two hours. We may grow to love it, though, when we get more players to try it out with.<br /> <br /> I think my ideal game would probably be something like Masquiem -- with Kindred Senses, Lashing Out and Disciplines that start off powerful but then refine that power in interesting ways. If I added in Paths of Enlightenment, that would be my perfect system. Lashing Out and Kindred Senses make for vampires that really feel like vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T02:42:36-08:00","id":1467034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1466490#post1466490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Good shout. I'm likely to separate Oblivion back into Necromancy and Obtenebretion anyway. As a Wraith player, I feel the Abyss should never have been conflated with the Underworld. Obtenebretion loses so much that way and you end up with some weird results (Hecata with Obtenebretion, Lasombra with Necromancy) that undermines the feel of both clans. (YMMV, etc.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would have suggested that but I was unsure how far you wanted to go. On a practical level it's remarkably simple to re separate them as the fusion is largely artificial and based on a disdain for unique disciplines rather than any thematic , gameplay or lore links. If anything its easier to run since you don't have a load of powers incoherently stapled together and the headache of an in game retcon of no benefit.<br /> <br /> Edit:as a side I actually shifted back the revised lasombra flaw of no reflection and increased damage since the tech flaw is pretty silly when you pull at it and just means every lasombra pc has a ghoul taking her calls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-07-2021, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T23:46:00-08:00","id":1467156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1467034#post1467034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would have suggested that but I was unsure how far you wanted to go. On a practical level it's remarkably simple to re separate them as the fusion is largely artificial and based on a disdain for unique disciplines rather than any thematic , gameplay or lore links. If anything its easier to run since you don't have a load of powers incoherently stapled together and the headache of an in game retcon of no benefit.<br /> <br /> Edit:as a side I actually shifted back the revised lasombra flaw of no reflection and increased damage since the tech flaw is pretty silly when you pull at it and just means every lasombra pc has a ghoul taking her calls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree with all of this. V5 puts in place ways that you have to learn the Hecata Oblivion powers to do Ceremonies anyway, so they're effectively two Disciplines sharing an umbrella anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T03:15:55-08:00","id":1467159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466468-v5-what-breaks-if?p=1467156#post1467156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I agree with all of this. V5 puts in place ways that you have to learn the Hecata Oblivion powers to do Ceremonies anyway, so they're effectively two Disciplines sharing an umbrella anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> The tricky part is if I'm going to do the same with blood sorcery. So far the only change I know I'm doing is changing the name back to thaumturgy for tremere since the name sticks out like a sore thumb amid names like potence and Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}